<title>FRANCE: Thomson &quot;notes&quot; new privatisation plan.</title>
<headline>Thomson &quot;notes&quot; new privatisation plan.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>French state-owned electronics company Thomson SA said on Thursday it took note of the government's decision to continue the firm's privatisation, with the priority being given to the sale of its Thomson-CSF defence subsidiary.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not have any particular comment. We take note of the finance ministry's decision,&quot; a Thomson spokesman said.</p>
<p>The government said on Wednesday night it has decided to sell separately Thomson-CSF and consumer electronics firm Thomson Multimedia in its privatisation of the Thomson group.</p>
<p>The terms for the Thomson-CSF sale are due to be announced in the next few days and the actual sale should take place in the first few months of 1997, the ministry statement said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 frs/pnt</p>
